# 🍎 Fruit Catcher — Design Prompt

## Overview
Fruit Catcher is a single-player arcade catch game for the web. The player controls a
basket at the bottom of the screen and slides it left/right to catch fruit that falls
from the top. The goal is to maximize score before running out of lives. It is built
as one self-contained HTML5 game with no dependencies, frameworks, or external assets.

## Core Loop
- Fruit spawns at the top and falls toward the basket at increasing speed over time.
- The player moves the basket horizontally to catch fruit in its opening.
- Catching fruit increases the score and grows a **combo** multiplier.
- Bombs also fall; catching one costs a life and resets the combo.
- Missing a fruit breaks the combo but does not cost a life.
- The run ends when all 3 lives are lost.

## Player Controls
- Keyboard: `←` / `→` or `A` / `D` to move; `Space` / `Enter` to pause and resume.
- Touch / Mouse: press and drag horizontally anywhere on the play field.
- Input must be smooth, responsive, and work on both desktop and mobile viewports.

## Scoring & Progression
- Each fruit is worth a base of 10 points multiplied by the current combo factor
  (up to 3× at high combos).
- Combos increase with each consecutive catch and reset on a miss or bomb.
- Difficulty ramps with elapsed time: fall speed and bomb frequency both rise, while
  spawn interval shrinks — so runs naturally accelerate.

## Power-Ups (occasional)
- ❤️ **Heart** — grants one extra life (capped at 5).
- 🕓 **Clock** — triggers slow-motion for several seconds, easing fall speed.
- ★ **Golden fruit** — a rare bonus catch worth extra points and a strong combo boost.

## Visual Direction
- Dark, animated gradient "orchard at night" background with drifting leaves and
  glowing fireflies (ambient canvas layer).
- Glassmorphic HUD showing Score, Best, Combo, and Lives.
- Gradient title and buttons; glowing, cohesive fruit, basket, and bomb visuals.
- Juice: catch particles, floating score popups, screen flash on bombs, and a brief
  screen shake when hit. Cohesive green/gold/fruit palette, no external assets.

## Technical Requirements
- Vanilla JavaScript (ES2020+) wrapped in an IIFE; `requestAnimationFrame` loop.
- HTML5 `<canvas>` for rendering; `localStorage` for the persistent best score.
- No frameworks, no CDN, no build step; all graphics and effects drawn in code.
- Must be fully playable and bug-free in modern browsers; delta-time updates clamped
  to avoid tunneling when the tab is backgrounded.

## Deliverables
- `index.html`, `style.css`, `game.js`, `README.md`, `README_fa.md`, `LICENSE`,
  `package.json`, `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`, and an English `Prompt` file.
- One-line summary: *A cozy, dependency-free HTML5 catch game — slide a glowing basket
  to collect fruit, chain combos, dodge bombs, and grab power-ups for a high score.*
